<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Phenomenon> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "High- and low-context cultures" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hall's contexting model" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "contexting" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "high-context and low-context communication" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "high-context culture" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "low-context culture" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/intercultural-communication> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Edward T. Hall's contrast between communication in which most meaning sits in shared context, relationships and nonverbal cues (high-context) and communication in which meaning is carried mainly by explicit words (low-context); widely taught for intercultural work, but its country rankings have weak empirical support." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/high-and-low-context-cultures> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/cross-cultural-communication> .
