<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who will read or hear this - including people copied or forwarded to - and which of them is the one who must act?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What does my primary audience already know, and which of my terms or steps would they not recognise?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What is in this for them, and do they see it in the first few lines?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I checked my picture of the audience against something they actually said or did, or am I only guessing?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "Subject: Data migration finishing three weeks later than planned (no change to cost). The move to the new reporting system will finish on 4 December instead of 13 November. Your month-end reports will run on the old system as usual until then. Technical details for your IT team are in the section below." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Heads up - the ETL refactor slipped because the CDC connector kept OOMing on the backfill. New ETA is sprint 14, assuming infra gets us the bigger nodes." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "An engineering lead emails a delay notice about a data-platform migration to a list that includes the client's finance director." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The finance director is the primary reader and needs the date, the impact on her work and the cost; the jargon and team shorthand move to a separate section for the technical secondary audience." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "List every audience, not just the addressee - the decision maker, technical reviewers, people who are copied, people the message may be forwarded to and people affected by the outcome." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "For the primary audience, write down what they already know, what they care about, what attitude they are likely to bring and what they must decide or do after reading." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Check your assumptions against evidence - the questions people actually ask you, past replies, usage data or a short conversation with a typical reader." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose content, order, vocabulary, tone and channel to fit the primary audience, putting what matters to them first." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Give secondary audiences their own clearly labelled section instead of mixing material for different readers." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Reread the draft as each audience in turn - including someone it might be forwarded to - and fix what would confuse or alienate them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Audience analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis/howto/3> .
