  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Audience analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "audience profiling" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "know your audience" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "reader analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The practice of working out, before you write or speak, who will receive a message, what they already know, what they care about and what they need to do with it, and then shaping the content, structure, tone and channel to fit them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/foundations> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Audience analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/bottom-line-up-front> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/audience-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/channel-selection> .
