<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could the other person have answered my question with one word, and was that what I really wanted?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did my next question build on their answer, or did I jump to my own agenda?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I ask a \"why\" question where a \"what\" or \"how\" would have felt less like a demand for justification?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When I needed a firm answer on a specific risk, did I ask a direct, specific question instead of a vague one?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "What's the part of the migration you're least confident about right now?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "Is the migration still on track for the end of the month?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead checks in with an engineer on a database migration that has gone quiet for a week." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The closed question invites a reflexive \"yes\"; the open one asks for an explanation and presumes there is some uncertainty, which makes it easier to surface a problem early." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Decide what you actually need to learn - their view, the obstacles, the options - before you ask anything." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Open with \"what\" or \"how\" (\"What's getting in the way?\", \"How did the client react?\") instead of \"Is\", \"Do\" or \"Did\"." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Stop talking and let them answer fully; resist offering a suggested answer if they pause." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Build your next question on what they just said (\"You mentioned the handover - what happened there?\") rather than switching topic." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Reflect back what you heard before asking another question, so the exchange does not become an interrogation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Switch to a closed or specific question when you need a commitment, a number, or a straight answer to a known risk (\"Will this slip past the 30th?\")." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Open-ended questions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions/howto/3> .
