  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/psychological-safety/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Psychologically safe teams can incubate bad behaviour" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/psychological-safety/s6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/psychological-safety/s6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#sourceType> "institutional" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/psychological-safety/s6> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.bps.org.uk/research-digest/psychologically-safe-teams-can-incubate-bad-behaviour-0> .
}

<https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do I know concretely what I will do tomorrow if this negotiation ends without a deal?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I compared my alternative with the offer on equivalent terms, or only on the headline price?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is my opening ask set by my goal, or have I let a weak alternative drag it down?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is everything I am about to say about my alternatives true?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "We've priced a comparable tool that would cost us about 8% less in year one, including migration. We'd rather stay - the team knows your product - so we're looking for a renewal at last year's rate with the new reporting module included. What would make that work on your side?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "We really can't move away from you, so please do what you can on the price. What's the best you can offer?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "An operations manager is renegotiating an annual software contract after the vendor proposes a 12% price rise." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The manager did the BATNA homework first (a real, like-for-like competing quote), so the ask is anchored on a goal rather than on desperation, the alternative is mentioned truthfully without a threat, and the question invites the vendor to solve the problem with them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before the first meeting, list every realistic thing you could do if no deal is reached - other vendors, other candidates, building it in-house, waiting, or doing nothing." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Translate each alternative into the same terms as the deal on the table (total cost, scope, risk, timing, effort to switch) so you are comparing like with like." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Pick the single best alternative - that is your BATNA - and from it set your reservation value, the worst deal you would still accept over walking away." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Spend some preparation time improving the BATNA itself (get a real competing quote, line up a second option) rather than only describing it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Estimate the other side's BATNA too, and ask about their alternatives, so you know how much they need this deal." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Anchor your opening ask on your goal, not on your BATNA; keep a weak BATNA to yourself and never invent an alternative you do not have." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/7> <https://schema.org/position> "7"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/7> <https://schema.org/text> "Re-check the BATNA whenever new information arrives during the talks, and walk away only when an offer is genuinely worse than it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "BATNA" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna/howto/7> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BATNA" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "best alternative to a negotiated agreement" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "developing your BATNA" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "walk-away alternative" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/negotiation-preparation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/principled-negotiation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Working out, before you negotiate, the best thing you will actually do if this negotiation fails - and using that alternative as the yardstick for every offer, the basis of your walk-away point and a source of leverage you can deliberately improve." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/negotiation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BATNA" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/anchoring-and-adjustment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/first-offer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/reservation-value> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/batna> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/zone-of-possible-agreement> .
