  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/teach-back/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Simple communication technique may improve health outcomes among diabetes patients" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/teach-back/s6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/teach-back/s6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#sourceType> "academic" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/source/teach-back/s6> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.ucsf.edu/news/2003/01/97177/simple-communication-technique-may-imrpove-health-outcomes-among-diabetes> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I ask them to say it in their own words, or did I accept a nod or a \"makes sense\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I frame the check as testing my explanation, not their competence?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which one or two points would cause real damage if misunderstood, and did I check those?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When their restatement was off, did I re-explain differently rather than repeat myself louder?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#after> "I've thrown a lot at you, so let me check I explained it well. If the patch fails on Thursday, what are your next two moves, and who hears from you first?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#before> "So that's the background - escalate to Priya's team if the patch fails, and keep the client posted. Does that all make sense?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead hands over an urgent client escalation to a colleague before going on leave." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#why> "The yes/no check invites a polite \"yes\"; the open request surfaces the missing piece (who to call first) while the lead can still fix it, and frames any gap as the explainer's problem." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Pick the one to three points the other person must get right to act - a deadline, a decision, a sequence of steps - rather than checking everything." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Explain each point in plain, specific language, one point at a time." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Take ownership of the check out loud, for example \"I want to make sure I explained that clearly.\"" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask an open request to restate or demonstrate (\"How will you walk the client through this?\"), never a yes/no question such as \"Does that make sense?\"" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Listen for gaps or errors; if you hear one, re-explain that part differently and ask again until their version is accurate." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Close by confirming the agreed version in writing where it matters (a recap message or ticket)." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Teach-back" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Teach-back" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "closing the loop on understanding" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "show-me method" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "teach-back method" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/checking-understanding> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Checking whether an explanation landed by asking the other person to explain it back, or show it, in their own words - framed as a test of how clearly you explained rather than of what they know - and re-explaining until their version is right." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/scheme/questioning-and-conversation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Teach-back" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/curse-of-knowledge> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/illusion-of-transparency> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/open-ended-questions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/teach-back> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/communication-graph/id/paraphrasing> .
